Patch sharing
-------------

Definitions

  "Patch" means a file in the .zvuky format, or any other description of a
  graph of the Software's modules, that the Software loads, renders or plays.

  "Work" means anything you make available to the public or to any third
  party, free of charge or not: for example a game, an application, a video,
  a recording, a sound pack, a sample library or a stream.

  A Patch is "used in a Work" when the Work contains the Patch, or contains
  sound that the Software produced from the Patch, whether rendered in advance
  or while the Work runs.

  "Library" means the public patch library at
  https://www.pekelec.eu/zvuky/knihovna.html, or its successor announced at
  that address or in the Software's official repository.

Obligation

  For every Patch used in a Work, you shall upload that Patch to the Library
  no later than 30 days after the Work is first made available. Upload the
  Patch in the version the Work uses. Attach the audio samples the Patch reads
  (Sampler module) if you have the right to share them; if you do not, name
  their source in the description of the upload.

Licence of uploaded Patches

  By uploading a Patch you license it to everyone under the Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Attached samples keep their
  own licence.

Exceptions

  You do not have to upload:
  (a) a Patch that is not used in any Work: private use, experiments, tests;
  (b) a Patch downloaded from the Library and used unchanged;
  (c) a Patch distributed together with the Software, used unchanged.

Fulfilment

  The obligation is fulfilled by submitting the Patch to the Library. If the
  Library rejects or later removes a submission, you are not in breach. If the
  Library cannot accept uploads for more than 30 days, the obligation is
  fulfilled by publishing the Patch under CC BY 4.0 at any publicly accessible
  place and naming that place in the documentation or credits of the Work.

Languages

  A Czech version of this licence follows. Both versions have the same
  meaning; in case of doubt, the Czech version prevails.


